// COVERS DatabricksLexerGrammar: Databricks, hostname, port, protocol, httpPath
//
// The whole grammar: five tokens, one datasource specification, every field optional in the
// grammar (DatabricksParserGrammar.g4:13 is a `( ... )*` alternation) and all four required
// by the walker. Syntax copied from TestDatabricksConnectionGrammarRoundtrip.
//
// `port` here is a STRING, not an integer literal -- upstream's own test writes
// `port: 'port';`, a non-numeric value, and it parses, so unlike MemSql's `port` this one is
// not converted at parse time. A numeric-looking value is used anyway; the point of the note
// is that `hostname`/`port` are Databricks' spellings and are NOT interchangeable with the
// `host`/`port` pair of the Static or MemSql specs, which are different grammars.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::dbx::Conn
{
   store: fixture::dbx::Db;
   type: Databricks;
   specification: Databricks
   {
      hostname: 'dbc-1234.cloud.databricks.com';
      port: '443';
      protocol: 'https';
      httpPath: '/sql/1.0/endpoints/abc123';
   };
   auth: ApiToken
   {
      apiToken: 'token';
   };
}
